WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.590
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.160
Oh man.
Hello.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:04.880
Thanks so much for coming.
Nah, thanks for having me.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.330
It's like 11, what is it, 24 hours ago

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.860
I think I found out I was
going to be or something.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:09.693
Oh, that's cool.
Yeah.

00:00:09.693 --> 00:00:10.880
It was nice of you to
come by and help us out.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.980
Exactly, I should have
brought my good razor.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.171
(audience laughing)

00:00:14.171 --> 00:00:15.004
(laughs) You could have helped us out.

00:00:15.004 --> 00:00:15.837
It would have gone a little faster.

00:00:15.837 --> 00:00:16.956
[Macaulay] Exactly.

00:00:16.956 --> 00:00:18.560
I think you'd look good if
half your head was shaved.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.543
What do you think, crowd?

00:00:19.543 --> 00:00:20.824
That's what everyone's saying backstage.

00:00:20.824 --> 00:00:22.331
(crowd cheering and applauding)

00:00:22.331 --> 00:00:23.567
No, no, no, that's all right.

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:24.780
You know, I want to ask you something.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.390
Actually we've worked
together a little bit

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:29.980
outside of this project
here at the Late Night show.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.170
And I never got to ask you this before

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.530
and it must be annoying, but
you must still get people

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.790
that even though you've
achieved a lot of great things

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.020
acting as an adult, you
must still get people

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.840
that can't let go of
the "Home Alone" thing

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.857
and come up to you and ask
for the "Home Alone" face.

00:00:43.857 --> 00:00:45.560
Yeah, no, I get it a good amount.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.397
And I just basically say to
them, "You know what, it's sad.

00:00:47.397 --> 00:00:48.910
"You don't want to see it."
(Conan laughing)

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.517
It'd be like, it's really
pathetic, he's old.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:51.657
You know, what happened, you know?

00:00:51.657 --> 00:00:53.370
Right, right, right, right.
So yeah.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.787
No, that's the good--
Yeah, exactly so.

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.380
People that are like, what do you expect?

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.240
Like, you'll be doing
that in clubs going around

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.073
doing that, it's like...
Exactly.

00:00:59.073 --> 00:01:01.980
Give people the wrong impression, exactly.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.410
You actually still have a
scar on you, I've been told,

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.886
that you got from Joe Pesci
shooting "Home Alone."

00:01:08.886 --> 00:01:09.750
Is that true?
Yeah.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:10.810
It's on my finger, yeah.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.530
It's actually one of the scenes, you know,

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.560
they hang me up on the
closet door or something.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.187
They said, "I'm gonna bite
each one of your fingers off

00:01:16.187 --> 00:01:19.423
"one at a time" and during
rehearsal he actually bit me.

00:01:19.423 --> 00:01:20.821
(audience laughing)

00:01:20.821 --> 00:01:21.870
And it broke the skin and everything.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.290
I'm a little nine-year-old boy

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.487
and he's going around
biting 'em, you know?

00:01:24.487 --> 00:01:26.330
And I still have the scar.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:27.760
I didn't even realize it until recently

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.270
and there it is, the little thing.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:33.650
Now, did you get mad
when Joe Pesci bit you?

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.940
Yes, I did, I got really mad at him.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:37.750
I was like, I don't care
how many Oscars you have

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.300
or whatever, like, don't.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.810
Biting a nine year old, what
the heck's wrong with you?

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.520
I love the idea of you just blowing up

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:44.543
on the set of that movie.
Yeah, it was like, hey.

00:01:44.543 --> 00:01:46.330
Well also, they hang me up on a door

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.110
so I'm also hanging on
a door at the same time

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:49.083
so I'm like, "What are you doing?"

00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:51.000
(Conan and audience laughing)

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.090
Probably not the most threatening

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:52.923
you've ever been in your life.

00:01:52.923 --> 00:01:53.756
Yeah, yeah, "Who do you think you are?"

00:01:53.756 --> 00:01:54.865
Kicking your legs, "I'll get you!"

00:01:54.865 --> 00:01:57.030
(audience laughing)

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.550
There's a dark side I wanna explore.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.602
You've hung out some with Marilyn Manson.

00:02:02.602 --> 00:02:03.435
Yes, yeah.

00:02:03.435 --> 00:02:04.340
Let's talk about that of course.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:06.160
He was in "Party Monster" with me.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.330
Yeah, and his character smoked in it

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.950
so he kind of wanted to learn
how to smoke and so he--

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.070
Marilyn Manson didn't know how to smoke?

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:13.903
He didn't know how to smoke.

00:02:13.903 --> 00:02:15.320
Never smoked a day in his life, he said.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.158
You know, the king, the
antichrist, you know?

00:02:17.158 --> 00:02:18.370
Yeah, yeah.
He didn't know how to smoke.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.485
He's like, well, it's not healthy.

00:02:19.485 --> 00:02:22.930
(audience laughing)
Exactly.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:23.763
Praise the devil.

00:02:23.763 --> 00:02:24.596
Want a cigarette?

00:02:24.596 --> 00:02:25.622
No, it's not healthy.

00:02:25.622 --> 00:02:29.872
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.017
So you know, he had this
very specific vision

00:02:34.017 --> 00:02:36.150
of what kind of cigarettes
he wanted in his mind.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.720
So he wanted me, the avid
smoker to go with him

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.902
and help him out and
so we go to the store.

00:02:40.902 --> 00:02:44.040
Basically, he wanted Virginia
Slims 100's basically.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.057
And so that was what he
wanted so we got him--

00:02:46.057 --> 00:02:48.527
Virginia Slims?
Virginia Slim 100's.

00:02:48.527 --> 00:02:50.140
Isn't that kind of an old lady cigarette?

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.010
Exactly, but it was
what he saw in his head

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:53.020
so I said, "Okay, cool."

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.430
And I just remember we were
walking out of the store.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.440
I mean, it's like, he's six
foot five and I'm, you know,

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.400
five foot (mumbles) and so
(audience laughing)

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.410
yeah, I just remember he turned to me.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.470
It was just this weird silence.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.500
He goes, "You know, that's
a Conan O'Brien story."

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.333
He was like, "You gotta make sure

00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:07.730
you tell that on Conan O'Brien"

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:10.600
that I was corrupting the
antichrist, so, you know.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.340
I love that Macaulay Culkin
is convincing, you know,

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.020
Marilyn Manson to have a cigarette.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.634
Exactly, go ahead, it's fine.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.790
(audience laughing)
What's happened?

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:21.267
Now, let's talk about this movie "Saved!"

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.400
"Saved!"
This is an interesting idea.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.410
It takes place at a Christian high school.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.700
Yeah, kind of a Christian high school

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.910
set in this kind of modern Christian town.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.690
And it's kind of just, I don't know,

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.990
it's a fun, funny kind of dark comedy.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:36.310
Right, right, it's--
With a fantastic ensemble.

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.021
How did you prepare for this movie?

00:03:38.021 --> 00:03:40.290
Did you hang out at all
with Christian groups?

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.046
Yeah, we went to a bunch of youth rallies

00:03:43.046 --> 00:03:44.670
and Christian rock concerts.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.583
And we went to this big one at,

00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:47.590
I think it's Edison Field in Anaheim

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:49.570
where the Angels play and it's, you know,

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:52.760
it was like the U2 soundalike rock band

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.580
or the Radiohead soundalike rock band.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.590
They're all Christian rock bands.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:56.860
They sound like those bands,

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:57.900
but then they just throw in stuff

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.090
about the loaves and the fishes.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.527
Exactly, it's kind of
uplifting, exactly, you know.

00:04:01.527 --> 00:04:03.720
And 40,000 born-again Christians

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.120
who are all blond, by the way.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.430
Just this sea of blond
born-again Christians.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.570
And I just remember
walking out of that place

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:13.420
and it was just weird 'cause
there was people picketing

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.310
and they were passing out all
these leaflets like, you know,

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.950
don't got to this, it's terrible

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.170
and it was other Christians.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:20.381
These other Christians were
picketing these other Christians

00:04:20.381 --> 00:04:22.573
and they picketing each other.
And they were mad

00:04:22.573 --> 00:04:24.960
that these Christians were
enjoying some rock music

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.230
that even had a Christian theme?

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:27.450
Exactly, exactly.
That seems odd.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.000
So I just thought it was
weird that, you know,

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.280
the Christians are picketing each other.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.260
I think we can get away
with doing a dark comedy

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:33.810
about them, you know?
Right.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:34.643
But we'll see.

00:04:34.643 --> 00:04:36.650
I mean, I think a good amount
of the Christian community

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.190
has actually kind of
responded to the movie

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.940
which is very good, very good to see.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:42.460
Did you get recognized at
the big Christian rock show?

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:43.360
Yes, that was funny, you know,

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.980
'cause it wasn't that
normal like, oh, do the face

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.677
or, you know, it was this kind of like,

00:04:47.677 --> 00:04:49.300
"We're so glad you're here!"

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.952
You know, they really
thought like, you know.

00:04:50.952 --> 00:04:51.785
(audience laughing)

00:04:51.785 --> 00:04:52.970
I didn't want to break
their hearts and like,

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.770
yeah, I'm just here for
research or something, you know?

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.210
But it was just this, it was amazing.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.300
They were just so happy
to see me there, you know?

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.890
Just like, they thought I
was one of them. (chuckles)

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:03.570
Right, right.
(audience laughing)

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.572
You sneaky bastard.
That's me.

